+++ b/docs/V168_GUARD_FUNCTION_ATTESTATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+# V168 Guard Function Attestation
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.168-guard-function-attestation`
+
+## Change
+
+Portal startup and the external PostgreSQL readiness gate now use one frozen
+contract for the five unique functions behind the nine protected database
+triggers. The contract verifies the canonical SHA-256 of `pg_proc.prosrc` and
+the function schema, name, identity arguments, language, trigger return type,
+kind, volatility, parallel safety, security mode, leakproof flag, strict flag,
+set-returning flag and per-function configuration.
+
+Migration `0123-guard-function-schema-binding` performs the one-time v168
+upgrade of all five guard functions. It pins each function to
+`search_path=pg_catalog, pg_temp`; the four acceptance functions resolve their
+ledger tables through `TG_TABLE_SCHEMA` and identifier-quoted dynamic SQL.
+This prevents a session-local `pg_temp` table from shadowing the protected
+ledger while preserving production and custom restore schemas.
+
+The attestation also verifies that each trigger has no `WHEN` clause, no
+arguments, no transition tables, no constraint binding and no parent trigger.
+The existing enabled state, event shape, table binding, function binding and
+update-column checks remain active.
+
+Function source canonicalization changes CRLF line endings to LF and trims
+outer whitespace only. Every internal source byte remains part of the hash.
+Schema binding remains relative to the table schema during startup, so an
+isolated restore rehearsal can use its custom schema. The external readiness
+gate continues to require the production `public` schema.
+
+## Failure behavior
+
+Attestation runs after migration `0123-guard-function-schema-binding` and before
+directory seeding and `COMMIT`. The 0123 upgrade creates the hardened function
+definitions once. After its migration marker exists, any function-body,
+function-metadata or trigger metadata drift aborts startup and rolls back the
+transaction without replacing or repairing the drifted definition.
+
+The PostgreSQL 18 isolation suite replaces an expected function body under the
+same name, changes security/configuration/volatility metadata, and adds trigger
+`WHEN` and argument drift. Each case must fail closed, remain drifted after the
+failed startup, be explicitly restored, and then pass attestation. It also
+proves that an extra differently named trigger is rejected and that a `pg_temp`
+shadow ledger cannot redirect the acceptance guards.
+
+## Provenance and scope
+
+The previous `0120` definition originated in baseline commit `fb9c96d`; the
+previous `0122` definitions originated in the v165 commit `091507b`. Historical
+0122 stays unchanged. Migration 0123 updates the four acceptance function
+bodies and fixes `proconfig` on all five functions while preserving their guard
+rules.
+
+- no table, column, backup format or backup data-contract change;
+- the required migration set adds 0123, while the backup manifest/schema
+  version remains `0122-acceptance-ledger-integrity` with 76 tables;
+- no payment, payout, wallet, game-provider, DNS, credential, plan or
+  production-control change;
+- no live provider or customer transaction calls during validation.
